problem:
Find the number of ordered pairs of integers $(a, b)$ such that the following equations hold:
\[
\begin{cases}
a^3 + b^3 = 180 \\
ab = 27
\end{cases}

Find all real numbers $k$ for which the following system of equations has a unique solution:
\[
\begin{cases}
x^2 + y^2 + kxy = 25 \\
x^2 - y^2 + kx^2y = 7
\end{cases}

在平面直角坐标系中，点 \(P(x, y)\) 和点 \(Q(u, v)\) 满足条件：对于所有实数 \(t\)，\[
|2x + 3y - t| + |u - v + t| \leq 3\sqrt{13}
\] 求线段 \(PQ\) 的最大可能长度。

On an equilateral triangle $ABC$, with side length 6, three circles are drawn, each tangent to two sides of the triangle and to two other circles, as shown below. The centers of these circles lie on the three altitude lines from vertices $A$, $B$, and $C$. What is the radius of each circle?

[asy]
import markers;
unitsize(2 cm);

pair A, B, C, I, J, K;
real r;
r = sqrt(3)/2;

A = (0,0);
B = (1,0);
C = rotate(60)*(B);
I = extension(A, reflect(A,B)*(C), B, reflect(B,C)*(A));
J = extension(B, reflect(B,C)*(A), C, reflect(C,A)*(B));
K = extension(C, reflect(C,A)*(B), A, reflect(A,B)*(C));

draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(Circle(I,r));
draw(Circle(J,r));
draw(Circle(K,r));

label("$A$", A, SW);
label("$B$", B, SE);
label("$C$", C, NW);
label("$I$", I, NE);
label("$J$", J, NW);
label("$K$", K, SW);
[/asy]

The function \(f(x)\) satisfies the equation
\[f(x^2 + y^2) + f(x^2 - y^2) = 4x^2f(y) + 2f(x^2)y^2 - 1\]
for all real numbers \(x\) and \(y\). Find all possible values of \(f(5).\)

There exists a unique sequence of positive integers $a_1,a_2,\cdots,a_{n+2}$ such that $a_1=a_{n+2}=0$ and
\begin{align*}
a_{i+1}=a_{i}^2+a_{i}+i,\quad i=1,\,2,\,3,\cdots,n
\end{align*}
Find the smallest positive integer n such that $a_{n+1}>2013$.

What is the smallest positive integer  $n$  such that the following can be verified as an integer:



( $b$  odd)
\[\sum_{k = 0}^{\lfloor{\frac{3n + 10}{8}\rfloor}}(-1)^k\cdot\dfrac{\binom{2n - 3k}{n}}{\binom{2n - 3k}{k}}\]\[\left(\dfrac{b + 1}{b} \right)\dfrac{\left(\dfrac{2b^n}{3n + 10b} \right)_{n + 2}}{\left(\dfrac{2b^n}{3n + 10b} \right)_{n + 3}}\right)?\]其中\dfrac{2b^n}{3n + 10b}表示\left(\dfrac{2b^n}{3n + 10b} \right)_k为下降阶乘\begin{equation*}
\prod_{j=0}^{k-1} \left( 1 - \frac{2b^n j}{3n + 10b j} \right) 
\end{equation*}\end{equation*}

A sequence \( a_n \) is defined as follows: \( a_1 = 1 \), and for all positive integers \( k \),
\[ a_{k+1} = \begin{cases} 
a_k + k & \text{if } k \text{ is odd,} \\
a_k / k & \text{if } k \text{ is even.}
\end{cases} \]
Find the smallest positive integer \( m \) such that \( a_m \) is an integer multiple of 2023.
